 (~85 per cycle). |\n| 2–3 | 6 | Every 3 days | ~2450 | 10 order days (600 in fees), but storage costs more. Quantities ~1.03–1.1× forecast. The warehouse limit is tight on shared arrival days. |\n| 4–7 | 4 | Every 4 days | ~2700–2900 | Only 7 order days, but highest storage cost and no carry-over buffer. Ordered at about the forecast, so short. It ordered 120 units of product 1 against ~160 demand on days 13–16. |\n| 4–7 | 7 | Every 3 days | ~2750 | Over-orders product 0 (1.24×), which then expires. Occasional overflow above the 152-unit limit. |\n| 4–7 | 5 | Every 2 days | ~2900–3100 | Orders 1.2–1.3× forecast. The steady surplus mostly expires. |\n| 4–7 | 0 | Every day | ~3000 | 28 order days cost 1680 in fees. Orders exactly the forecast, which is below mean demand. |\n| 8 | 1 | Every 2 days | Far worst | Never orders product 1, so it loses that profit and pays penalties every day. |"}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 5058, "cache_read_input_tokens": 886, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 5058}, "output_tokens": 8, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-29T08:11:00.800Z", "request_id": "req_011CgWBruKhoQYu3SjpXnk7R"}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_stop", "index": 1}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_start", "index": 2, "content_block": {"type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01CzHLF3F7ojmctcdZGXuZoA", "name": "StructuredOutput", "input": {}, "caller": {"type": "direct"}}}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CgWBruaaNgVDRT34WB3rZ", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "tool_u